1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Luke 23

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:07,060
Then the whole company of them arose and brought him before Pilate,

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,760
and they began to accuse him, saying,

4
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:13,740
We found this man misleading our nation

5
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:17,320
and forbidding us to give tribute to Caesar

6
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:23,000
and saying that he himself is Christ, a king.

7
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,080
And Pilate asked him,

8
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:27,820
Are you the king of the Jews?

9
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,760
And he answered him,

10
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:31,860
You have said so.

11
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:35,140
Then Pilate said to the chief priests and the crowds,

12
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:38,780
I find no guilt in this man.

13
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:40,980
But they were urgent, saying,

14
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:43,120
He stirs up the people,

15
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:47,140
teaching throughout all Judea from Galilee even to this place.

16
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:51,280
When Pilate heard this, he asked whether the man was a Galilean.

17
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:54,420
And when he learned that he belonged to Herod's jurisdiction,

18
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:56,640
he sent him over to Herod,

19
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:59,160
who was himself in Jerusalem at that time.

20
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:02,640
When Herod saw Jesus, he was very glad,

21
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:05,000
for he had long desired to see him,

22
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:06,660
because he had heard about him,

23
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:09,760
and he was hoping to see some sign done by him.

24
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,520
So he questioned him at some length,

25
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:13,980
but he made no answer.

26
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:18,340
The chief priests and the scribes stood by vehemently accusing him.

27
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:22,460
And Herod with his soldiers treated him with contempt and mocked him.

28
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:25,860
Then, arraying him in splendid clothing,

29
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,680
he sent him back to Pilate.

30
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:27,800
And Pilate said,

31
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:28,720
And Herod and Pilate said,

32
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:31,700
And Herod and Pilate became friends with each other that very day.

33
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:34,620
For before this they had been at enmity with each other.

34
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:39,260
Pilate then called together the chief priests and the rulers and the people,

35
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:40,380
and said to them,

36
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:45,420
You brought me this man as one who was misleading the people,

37
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,600
and after examining him before you,

38
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:54,720
behold, I did not find this man guilty of any of your charges against him,

39
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:58,640
neither did Herod, for he sent him back to us.

40
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:03,080
Look, nothing deserving death has been done by him.

41
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:06,900
I will therefore punish and release him.

42
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,720
But they all cried out together,

43
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:14,600
Away with this man, and release to us Barabbas.

44
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:19,620
A man who had been thrown into prison for an insurrection started in the city,

45
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:20,700
and for murder.

46
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,300
Pilate addressed them once more,

47
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:25,260
desiring to release Jesus,

48
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:26,520
but they kept shouting,

49
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,200
Crucify!

50
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:30,880
Crucify him!

51
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,280
A third time he said to them,

52
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:37,520
Why, what evil has he done?

53
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:41,780
I have found in him no guilt deserving death.

54
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:45,340
I will therefore punish and release him.

55
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,980
But they were urgent, demanding with loud cries that he should be crucified,

56
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,860
and their voices prevailed.

57
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:55,180
So Pilate decided that their demand should be granted.

58
00:02:55,860 --> 00:02:58,700
He released the man who had been thrown into prison for insurrection,

59
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,800
and murder, for whom they asked.

60
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,760
But he delivered Jesus over to their will.

61
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:07,880
And as they led him away, they seized one Simon of Cyrene,

62
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:09,760
who was coming in from the country,

63
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:13,060
and laid on him the cross to carry it behind Jesus.

64
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:16,280
And there followed him a great multitude of the people,

65
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:19,100
and of women who were mourning and lamenting for him.

66
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,480
But turning to them, Jesus said,

67
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,600
Daughters of Jerusalem,

68
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,140
do not weep for me,

69
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,100
but weep for yourselves,

70
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:29,700
and for your children.

71
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:33,940
For behold, the days are coming when they will say,

72
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,100
Blessed are the barren,

73
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:38,440
and the wombs that never bore,

74
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:40,960
and the breasts that never nursed.

75
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:45,540
Then they will begin to say to the mountains,

76
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:49,040
Fall on us, and to the hills,

77
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:50,740
cover us.

78
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:54,720
For if they do these things when the wood is green,

79
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:58,100
what will happen when it is dry?

80
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:02,880
Two others who were criminals were led away to be put to death with him.

81
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:06,180
And when they came to the place that is called the Skull,

82
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:08,700
there they crucified him and the criminals,

83
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,920
one on his right and one on his left.

84
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:12,400
And Jesus said,

85
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:17,400
Father, forgive them,

86
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:22,500
for they know not what they do.

87
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:26,100
And they cast lots to divide his garments.

88
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:28,120
And the people stood by watching,

89
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:30,120
but the rulers scoffed at him, saying,

90
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:32,120
He saved others.

91
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:34,120
Let him save himself,

92
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:36,120
if he is the Christ of God,

93
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:38,120
his chosen one.

94
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:40,120
The soldiers also mocked him,

95
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:42,120
coming up and offering him sour wine,

96
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:44,120
and saying,

97
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:46,120
If you are the king of the Jews,

98
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:48,120
save yourself.

99
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:50,120
There was also an inscription over him,

100
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:52,120
This is the king of the Jews.

101
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:54,120
One of the criminals who were hanged railed at him, saying,

102
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,120
This is the king of the Jews.

103
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:58,120
One of the criminals who were hanged railed at him, saying,

104
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:00,120
Are you not the Christ?

105
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:02,120
Save yourself and us.

106
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:05,120
But the other rebuked him, saying,

107
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:08,120
Do you not fear God,

108
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:13,120
since you are under the same sentence of condemnation?

109
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:16,120
And we indeed justly,

110
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:24,120
for we are receiving due reward of our deeds.

111
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:27,120
But this man has done nothing right.

112
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:30,120
And he said,

113
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:36,120
Jesus, remember me when you come into your kingdom.

114
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:38,120
And he said to him,

115
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:44,120
Truly I say to you,

116
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:52,120
today you will be with me in paradise.

117
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:54,120
It was now about the sixth hour,

118
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:56,120
and there was darkness over the whole land.

119
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:58,120
Until the ninth hour,

120
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,120
while the sun's light failed,

121
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:04,120
and the curtain of the temple was torn in two.

122
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:07,120
Then Jesus, calling out with a loud voice, said,

123
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:23,120
Father, into your hands I commit my spirit.

124
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:25,120
And having said this,

125
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:27,120
he breathed his last.

126
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:31,120
Now when the centurion saw what had taken place,

127
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,120
he praised God, saying,

128
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:36,120
Certainly this man was innocent.

129
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:40,120
And all the crowds that had assembled for this spectacle,

130
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:42,120
when they saw what had taken place,

131
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:45,120
returned home beating their breasts.

132
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:47,120
And all his acquaintances

133
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:50,120
and the women who had followed him from Galilee

134
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:53,120
stood at a distance watching these things.

135
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:55,120
Now there was a man named Joseph,

136
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:57,120
from the Jewish town of Arimathea.

137
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:59,120
He was a member of the council,

138
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:01,120
a good and righteous man,

139
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:04,120
who had not consented to their decision and action,

140
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:07,120
and he was looking for the kingdom of God.

141
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:11,120
This man went to Pilate and asked for the body of Jesus.

142
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:14,120
Then he took it down and wrapped it in a linen shroud,

143
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:16,120
and laid him in a tomb cut in stone,

144
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:19,120
where no one had ever yet been laid.

145
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:21,120
It was the day of preparation,

146
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:23,120
and the Sabbath was beginning.

147
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,120
The women who had come with him from Galilee

148
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:29,120
followed and saw the tomb and how his body was laid.

149
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:32,120
Then they returned and prepared spices and ointments.

150
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:35,120
On the Sabbath they rested according to the commandment.

